A||N||8||KRMFiero||84 Fiero SE 2M4||||5||
Z||000000||KRMFiero||09-26-2000||04:59 PM||||Okay, I am fixing up this '84 2M4 SE I got for my first car, the engine needs to be redone (rod knock) should I upgrade to a 3800? is so what stuff do i need out of the donor car? the interor needs some work... where can i get new seats with speakers in them?   someone told me that I could get a 200 mph spedo coversion kit? if so where, if not mine only says 85 do they make one that goes higher?    anything I should look into buying for this car?<P><BR>thanx alot<BR>Kyle||||reg||5
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-26-2000||05:05 PM||||The later GT's had a 120 mph speedo.  I'm not sure if it's a direct plug and play swap.  I think it is, just not for sure.<P>Someone here might have some grey 84 seats your looking for and that speedo, post a "Wanted" thread in the Mall section and see what comes up.<P>By the way, Welcome to the forum.<P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">         <BR>         <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||09-26-2000||05:25 PM||||Depends on where your car is from. I had great plans for my car, but there were so many small things wrong with it that I decided not to do any modifications. But a 3800 is very expensive. Especially since you are not going from a 2.8. An easier swap would be a 3.4, but even then I would assume you need a 2.8 donor car..? Someone correct me if I'm wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||09-27-2000||12:48 PM||||You are not limited to using 84 or 85 seats to get headrest speakers.  Take a look at Mr. Mike's page for instructions for installing headrest speakers to 86 - 88 seats.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com/addspeakers.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mrmikes.com/addspeakers.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||whamel||09-27-2000||01:45 PM||||I've seen some of those '200 mph speedo conversion kits' on Ebay.  I think if you do a search for Fiero and White faced gauge you'll find them.  Not sure though, but I think that's the guy.  Looks to just be a sticker kit you put on your old set.  I'm not sure personally, but at least that will get you started.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||09-27-2000||04:30 PM||||FOCOA sells a 200 mph speedo conversion kit.  It includes the sticker for the gauge face and a resister that needs to be replaced on the circuit board.  I think it costs around $50 or so.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero5||09-28-2000||08:50 PM||||I have heard that the 84's are the hardest to do an engine swap in, because of the wiring. But it is doable.<P>------------------<BR>           [IMG]file:///Go%20Bengals/Desktop%20Folder/Steve%27s%20Stuff/FamilyFieros-9%20copy[/IMG]||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-28-2000||09:02 PM||||I believe you don't have all the same holes for mounting engines in 84. That can be a pain. depends what you are changing to how much it matters.||||reg||1
Z||000008||tiacPaul||09-29-2000||07:33 AM||||My 84 started out about where you are at.  I recomend a good junk yard engine and then sell it before you spend too much fixing it up.  I say make it run, sell it, buy a newer one and fix it up,  you'll be much more pleased now since you can appreciate it.  That's all my 84 does,  make me wish i had an 88 GT!||||reg||13
